ting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260830-kp4zpu\n- **Title:** TASK-260830-kp4zpu: implement-provider-identity-validation\n- **Parent:** STORY-260830-315721\n\n### Description\n\nCreate and validate exact native session IDs, store roots, backend realms, build tuples, and discovery evidence. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\n\n### Scope\n\nrelux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); §2.4, §5.5, §7.5-7.7, §8. Work only inside the provider-identity-profile-and-resume story boundary.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nProduction behavior demonstrates: Create and validate exact native session IDs, store roots, backend realms, build tuples, and discovery evidence. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260830-kp4zpu_producer.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-kp4zpu/TASK-260830-kp4zpu_producer.md`\n\n- Byte count: `4790`\n- Content digest: `sha256:44183bd76c3fa76351810c61077b6f6b6d55b791017dcf7b1466b903c23d18a2`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-kp4zpu_reviewer-cr1.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-kp4zpu/TASK-260830-kp4zpu_reviewer-cr1.md`\n\n- Byte count: `5762`\n- Content digest: `sha256:7957f253bd3a06cfb7b78c881041db41721922facf82701cfc3fc06e8ab60d6f`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-kp4zpu_checkpoint-brief-rev1.md\nCheckpoint-only run for TASK-260830-kp4zpu (implement-provider-identity-validation, STORY-260830-315721). Change Request revision 1 was ACCEPTED by the independent reviewer RUN-260917-01e14c (TASK-260830-kp4zpu_review-verdict-rev1.md, tree 144f2b3 on base 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e, 13 paths); the leaf is a non-final Story leaf (siblings TASK-260830-3uzfyn and TASK-260830-2zvo8m follow), so the accepted candidate must become one internal signed checkpoint commit on the Story branch and the task must remain integrating. Do exactly this, from the control root /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager with the authoritative board: (1) read the board state (task integrating, CR rev1 accepted, checklist complete) and the verdict; (2) run `task-board worktree checkpoint TASK-260830-kp4zpu` (this run is the producer-bound integration run the command requires) and record its exact output and exit; (3) verify the result: `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-315721/worktree verify-commit HEAD` good signature for oparin@me.com, the commit's tree equals the accepted CR tree, its parent is 62d4463, `git status` in the Story worktree is clean apart from the board checkout artifact, `task-board worktree status` shows the CR checkpointed and the task integrating with integrationCheckpointed=true; (4) attach TASK-260830-kp4zpu_checkpoint-rev1.md as a task-scoped outcome with every comma